<title>GERMANY: FORD-WERKE SAYS 5-MONTH SALES, OUTPUT DOWN.</title>
<headline>FORD-WERKE SAYS 5-MONTH SALES, OUTPUT DOWN.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>First five months of</p>
<p>1997</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group sales				  11,100  down 5.5 pct</p>
<p>    Group vehicle output (in units)	394,500 down 11.9 pct</p>
<p>    Group vehicle sales (in units)	 456,700 down 9.5 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German carmaker is Ford-Werke AG</p>
<p>, a unit of U.S. carmaker Ford Motor Co.</p>
<p>The carmaker said in a statement that it had fulfilled its</p>
<p>goal of lowering costs by three percent of sales during the</p>
<p>five-month period.</p>
<p>Ford-Werke said it will be difficult to match 1996 sales</p>
<p>levels in 1997 but that it was hopeful to maintain its market</p>
<p>share at 11.3 percent.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
